      "side": 1,
      "message": "`libusb_get_device_descriptor` can fail and return an error code. If it fails, `desc` remains uninitialized, leading to a read of uninitialized memory on the next line when you check `idVendor` and `idProduct`.\n\n**Recommendation:**\nInitialize `desc` to zero and check the return value:\n```cpp\n\t\tstruct libusb_device_descriptor desc \u003d {0};\n\t\tif (libusb_get_device_descriptor(list.get()[i], \u0026desc) \u003d\u003d 0) {\n\t\t\tif (desc.idVendor \u003d\u003d vid \u0026\u0026 desc.idProduct \u003d\u003d pid) {\n\t\t\t\tcount++;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n```\n*(Please also apply this to the identical loop in `openDevice` below).*",
