      "side": 1,
      "message": "### Integer Promotion / Undefined Behavior Risk\n\nThe `uint8_t` values from `buff` are implicitly promoted to `int` (which is signed) before the bitwise shift. If `buff[i + 3]` has its highest bit set (e.g., `0x80`), shifting it by 24 bits into a signed `int` triggers undefined behavior ([before C++20](https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/operator_arithmetic)), and typically results in sign extension when added to the `uint32_t checksum`. This will corrupt the checksum calculation.\n\n**Recommendation:**\nExplicitly cast the bytes to `uint32_t` before shifting, exactly as you correctly did in `get32Le`:\n```cpp\n\t\tchecksum +\u003d static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(buff[i]) | \n\t\t\t    (static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(buff[i + 1]) \u003c\u003c 8) | \n\t\t\t    (static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(buff[i + 2]) \u003c\u003c 16) |\n\t\t\t    (static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(buff[i + 3]) \u003c\u003c 24);\n```",
      "revId": "641b544cc171ddb2904300e8cfb5e179163706ce",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
