      "side": 1,
      "message": "### Incomplete Cleanup and Early Return\n\n**Issue 1: Early Return on Failure**\nIf `libusb_release_interface` fails for one interface, you immediately `return -1;`. This skips the release of any remaining interfaces in `m_hidInterfaces`. Cleanup functions should generally make a best-effort attempt to release all resources.\n\n**Issue 2: Missing Kernel Driver Reattachment**\nAs noted in a previous review comment, if you detach a kernel driver during initialization, you should attempt to reattach it during cleanup using `libusb_attach_kernel_driver()`.\n\n**Recommendation:**\nContinue the loop even on failure, and attempt to reattach the kernel drivers:\n```cpp\n\tint ret \u003d 0;\n\tfor (size_t i \u003d 0; i \u003c m_hidInterfaces.size(); i++) {\n\t\tif (libusb_release_interface(m_devHandlePtr.get(),\n\t\t\t\t\t     m_hidInterfaces[i]) !\u003d 0) {\n\t\t\tlogInfo(\"[IAP] {} - release interface ({}) failed\\n\",\n\t\t\t\t__func__, m_hidInterfaces[i]);\n\t\t\tret \u003d -1;\n\t\t}\n\t\t// Make a best-effort attempt to reattach the kernel driver if we detached it earlier.\n\t\tlibusb_attach_kernel_driver(m_devHandlePtr.get(), m_hidInterfaces[i]);\n\t}\n\n\tm_devHandlePtr.reset();\n\n\tif (DEBUG_LOG)\n\t\tlogInfo(\"[IAP] {} - exit\\n\", __func__);\n\n\treturn ret;\n```",
      "revId": "641b544cc171ddb2904300e8cfb5e179163706ce",
